  "result": "I added `clamp` and its tests and committed them. `npm run fast` passed.\n\n- **`clamp`:** `src/cli/clamp.ts` exports `clamp(value, min, max)`. It throws a `RangeError` when `min > max`, and otherwise limits the value to the inclusive range.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/clamp.test.ts` covers a value inside the range, values below and above it, `min` equal to `max`, and the reversed-range error.\n- **Shard weight:** I added a weight of 0.1 for the new test file in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`, as the repo conventions require. That value is my guess, not a measured time.\n\n**Commit title:** The commit title is \"Add clamp that rejects a reversed range\" and has no task id. The conventions ask for the id in parentheses at the end, but my brief didn't include one and I didn't want to invent it. To add it, run `git commit --amend` with the id appended.",
